message: "Version 4.0.0, 12 September 2026. Identify the version and informal AI-review status when citing."
title: "Output-uniform positivity and explicit SoS size for simple bamboo"
authors:
  - name: "Quantyra Research"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: "For every Boolean output A at even q>=1024, m=q^2, N=8q+4 and D=floor(q/(32 log_2 q)), the specified simple-bamboo encoding has explicit real SoS refutation size at least (8/7)^((2D-1)/2). The proof checks arbitrary-output complete-row positivity and applies the credited restriction to residual width q. A separate indexed, encoding-specific generator corollary has seed length s=16q^3+8q^2 and output length q^4=Theta(s^(4/3)); in-range outputs are satisfiable and the refutation statement is vacuous there. The measure counts explicit multiplier/root monomials, not arithmetic circuits. Informal AI-reviewed mathematics; novelty and priority are unknown."
keywords:
  - weak rank principle
  - local distributions
  - conditional correlation
  - positivity
  - sum of squares
  - certificate size
  - proof complexity generators
